    "html": "<h1>The FORMAT</h1>\n<p>The FORMAT is the versioned contract of a GOLMET workspace: directory layout, artifact grammar and legal state transitions. It is the layer that survives engines, kits and releases.</p>\n<h2>Entities</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Entity</th>\n<th>What it holds</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>RN</td>\n<td>A numbered business rule — the versioned agreement with your client</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PEND</td>\n<td>An open question that never silently becomes scope</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CR</td>\n<td>A change request against an already-approved requirement</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Feature / Task</td>\n<td>Delivery units anchored on an active RN</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Spec</td>\n<td>Technical translation of the rules (data model, contracts, screens)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ADR</td>\n<td>The reason behind each decision</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Evidence</h2>\n<p>Every requirement cites its implementation: <code>[src/path/file.ts:42 @1ed8b81]</code>. The grammar is parseable by machine — the kit compares the hash against the repository HEAD and reports exactly what drifted.</p>\n<h2>Hard rules</h2>\n<p>Ten invariants (H1–H10) keep the workspace honest: a PEND never anchors a Feature, IDs are immutable, evidence must be parseable. <code>golmet validate</code> enforces them — exit code non-zero blocks CI.</p>\n",
